.TH TIM 1 "2026-09-29" "tim 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tim \- compile and run Tim programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tim
.RB [ build ]
.RI [ flags ]
.IR file .tim | dir
.br
.B tim run
.RI [ flags ]
.IR file .tim
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B tim test
.RI [ flags ]
.RI [ dir ]
.br
.B tim \-c
.I code
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tim
compiles Tim source to a native executable for Linux (amd64, arm64, riscv64),
Windows (amd64, arm64) or macOS (arm64), with no assembler or linker.
Given a directory, it compiles the directory's only non-test
.B .tim
file, or its
.BR main.tim .
Definitions a program uses but does not have are taken from the other
.B .tim
files of its directory.
.PP
.B run
compiles to a temporary file and runs it with
.IR args ,
exiting with the program's exit code.
.B test
compiles each
.BI * _test.tim
and
.BI test_ *.tim
file with a runner that calls its functions whose names start with
.BR test ;
a test fails if it returns an error value, exits with a nonzero code or stops
at a runtime error.
A file whose first line starts with
.B #!
runs as a script.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
The executable. The default is the source name without
.BR .tim ,
with
.B .exe
for Windows. An
.B .exe
name selects Windows.
.TP
.BI \-\-target " arch-os"
Cross-compile: amd64-linux, arm64-linux, riscv64-linux, amd64-windows,
arm64-windows or arm64-darwin.
.TP
.BI \-\-arch " arch" ", " \-\-os " os"
The target one part at a time.
.TP
.BI \-c " code"
Compile and run
.IR code .
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-watch
With
.BR run :
run again whenever a
.B .tim
file of the program's directory changes.
.TP
.B \-d
List the program's imports instead of compiling it.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Imported Git repositories are cached in
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/tim ,
or
.I ~/.cache/tim
when it is unset.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Print diagnostics without color.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
$ tim hello.tim && ./hello
$ tim run server.tim \-\-port 8080
$ tim \-c 'println(2 ** 100)'
$ tim \-\-target arm64\-darwin hello.tim
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
GRAMMAR.md and STDLIB.md in the Tim sources.
